{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":78928029,"ns":0,"title":"Implicit and explicit knowledge","extract":"Implicit and explicit knowledge are two contrasting types of knowledge often discussed in the field of second language acquisition (SLA). Implicit knowledge refers to the unconscious, intuitive knowledge that learners develop through meaningful exposure and use of a language.","description":"Types of linguistic knowledge","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}